app=Fractadyne
notes=The view that kept working after it settled (2026-10-20, beta.19 build 5374, RTX 3080, a 5120x2054 window): 2^704.7, auto-iterations at ~396,000, supersampled. Each walk's passes cost ~10 ms up to ~200,000 iterations and ~100x more where the pixels begin to escape (~219,900), and passes went out on quick frames four deep: in-flight passes to 1,865 ms, 24 samples in ~2 minutes. The battery's settle row (step 10) glides onto it and lets the supersampling converge.
